        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12464126/comment/12868113",
          "id": "12868113",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mreutegg",
            "name": "mreutegg",
            "key": "mreutegg",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658"
            },
            "displayName": "Marcel Reutegger",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "body": "I was wondering if it makes sense to build the StringCache right into the NameFactoryImpl, instead of using it before each call to getQName() ? Other modules might also benefit from such an optimization. WDYT?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mreutegg",
            "name": "mreutegg",
            "key": "mreutegg",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658"
            },
            "displayName": "Marcel Reutegger",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "created": "2010-05-17T07:27:38.688+0000",
          "updated": "2010-05-17T07:27:38.688+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12464126/comment/12868126",
          "id": "12868126",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=stefan%40jira",
            "name": "stefan@jira",
            "key": "stefan@jira",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Stefan Guggisberg",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "> I was wondering if it makes sense to build the StringCache right into the NameFactoryImpl, instead of using it before each call to getQName() ? Other modules might also benefit from such an optimization. WDYT?\n\nyes, maybe. however, i prefered to keep the scope of the changes for this issue local. \n\nusing StringCache in NameFactoryImpl should IMO be  proposed in a separate issue as it might cause unwanted side-effects (just my gut feeling ;)",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=stefan%40jira",
            "name": "stefan@jira",
            "key": "stefan@jira",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Stefan Guggisberg",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2010-05-17T08:06:47.962+0000",
          "updated": "2010-05-17T08:06:47.962+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12464126/comment/12868210",
          "id": "12868210",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mduerig",
            "name": "mduerig",
            "key": "mduerig",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=mduerig&avatarId=13834"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael D\u00fcrig",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Bucharest"
          },
          "body": "Looks good to me. Do the davex integration tests still pass with the patch applied?\n\nFurthermore, did you check the impact of the StringCache on memory and performance? There is a similar mechanism in place already for NameFactoryImpl which works on Name instances instead of Strings.\n\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mduerig",
            "name": "mduerig",
            "key": "mduerig",
